  "raw_text": "erently? User: Sorry can you repeat that? Agent: Certainly. If there was a deal on the Chick-fil-A chicken sandwich, what would you do differently? User: Um if there was a deal that made it the same price it is now or cheaper than I would get it. Agent: Okay, that makes sense. Over the past two weeks, what are your most common fast-food patterns? This includes when you eat it, what you usually order, and what typically triggers it. User: Um I have not gotten fast food in the past two weeks Agent: Thank you for that information. In your opinion, what does \"good value\" mean to you in fast food? User: . Um, It means you're able to get fresh hot and fairly inexpensive food quickly. Agent: Based on that, could you pick your top two or three factors from taste, portion size, speed, nutrition, consistency, and price, and explain how you judge if something is \"worth it\"? User: Taste is definitely the top one because if I don't like how it tastes I'm not going to get it. And price is the second",
